"""T-114j candidate: FB-EC4-Q24 (deployed D11 lineage) + the learned closure over the weight graph run closed-loop
(per-layer mean corrections from a message-passing model on the card's live state and the weights, carried into the
recursion with the consistent covariance). Numpy-free; the fnp functions are certified against the instrument.

Base docstring follows.
FB-EC4-Q24 with a target-free native raw20/sigma instrumentation seam.

The prediction recurrence below is copied from the exact near-floor-min Q24
source.  ``Estimator.predict`` follows the original path and still returns
only that prediction.  ``predict_with_native_tape`` enables additional
FlopScope-only observables from the same live Q24 state.  It contains no
reader, fit, target, score, retry, submission, absolute-path import, or
unmetered numerical library.

The twenty native fields intentionally retain the old CP1792 raw20 *field
definitions* but not its state values.  State-dependent fields are recomputed
from Q24's CP16384/EC4 closure.  This distinction is the transfer question;
the old CP1792 tape is neither read nor silently treated as Q24-native.

State after h_l (l < 16): fp64 mean/covariance, a full-birth fp32 CP3 state,
an fp32 cubic coordinate-star residual, a rank-2048 fp32 symmetric CP4
carrier, and an fp32 quartic coordinate-star plus one fp64 covariance-pairing
coefficient.
"""

